    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change required `POST /api/owners` (read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`) to return a `displayName` field formatted as `\"LastName, FirstName\"` from the stored names.\n\n**Two edits**, following the project's Spring/OpenAPI/MapStruct conventions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema. DTOs are code-generated from this spec at build time, so this produces the `displayName` getter/setter on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes the field:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n   `firstName`/`lastName` are both required (non-null) fields, so the concatenation is always well-formed.\n\n**Result:** `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).",
